{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-h1-reviewer-fable-36","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:e1c190d24275becc0db4","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names colony_id as the independent-unit column and defines one row as one colony assayed once, so the issue class would require some colony_id to contribute more than one row to the binomial test.","observed_value":"Independent unit column: colony_id; one row = one colony assayed once","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":18,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"One row is: one field-collected ant colony, assayed once in the two-cavity choice arena\nIndependent unit column: colony_id\nOne trial is: one row"}]},{"description":"The row-independent procedure applied is an exact binomial test computed over all data rows (n_rows), so each row entering it is one trial; repeated rows for the same colony would inflate the trial count.","observed_value":"binomtest(successes, n_rows, 0.5, two-sided) over all 20 rows","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":69,"end_line":70,"quoted_text":"    successes = choices.count(PREFERRED)\n    result = binomtest(successes, n_rows, NULL_P, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The input CSV contains exactly 20 data rows with 20 distinct colony_id values (TMN-01 through TMN-20); no colony_id appears on more than one row, so no independent unit enters the test more than once.","observed_value":"20 rows, 20 unique colony_id values, max 1 row per colony","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"TMN-01,Bracken Hollow,118,22.4,narrow,41.5\nTMN-02,Bracken Hollow,96,22.1,narrow,58.0\nTMN-03,Bracken Hollow,143,22.6,wide,73.2\nTMN-04,Bracken Hollow,102,22.3,narrow,36.9\nTMN-05,Bracken Hollow,127,22.5,narrow,49.4\nTMN-06,Sedge Knoll,88,21.9,narrow,62.7\nTMN-07,Sedge Knoll,134,22.2,wide,80.1\nTMN-08,Sedge Knoll,111,22.0,narrow,45.3\nTMN-09,Sedge Knoll,99,21.8,wide,91.6\nTMN-10,Sedge Knoll,125,22.4,narrow,38.2\nTMN-11,Alder Ridge,140,22.7,narrow,44.8\nTMN-12,Alder Ridge,107,22.5,narrow,52.1\nTMN-13,Alder Ridge,93,22.2,narrow,67.4\nTMN-14,Alder Ridge,152,22.8,wide,76.5\nTMN-15,Alder Ridge,116,22.6,narrow,40.0\nTMN-16,Quarry Copse,104,22.1,narrow,55.6\nTMN-17,Quarry Copse,131,22.3,narrow,47.9\nTMN-18,Quarry Copse,89,21.7,wide,84.3\nTMN-19,Quarry Copse,145,22.9,narrow,33.7\nTMN-20,Quarry Copse,113,22.4,narrow,59.2"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly verifies one row per colony before testing and aborts with an error if any colony_id repeats, so a repeated-unit entry cannot silently reach the binomial test.","observed_value":"check_one_row_per_colony raises SystemExit if any colony_id count exceeds 1","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":34,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"def check_one_row_per_colony(rows):\n    \"\"\"Confirm the file holds a single assayed row per colony.\"\"\"\n    per_colony = Counter(row[UNIT_COLUMN] for row in rows)\n    worst = max(per_colony.values())\n    if worst != 1:\n        repeated = sorted(cid for cid, k in per_colony.items() if k > 1)\n        raise SystemExit(\n            \"expected one assayed row per colony; repeated: \" + \", \".join(repeated)\n        )\n    return len(per_colony), worst"}]},{"description":"The report's stated design counts match the data: 20 rows analysed, 20 distinct colonies, and a maximum of one row contributed by any colony, confirming the test used exactly one observation per independent unit.","observed_value":"Rows analysed: 20; distinct colonies: 20; max rows per colony: 1","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":10,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"- Rows analysed: 20\n- Distinct colonies (colony_id): 20\n- Maximum rows contributed by any one colony: 1"}]},{"description":"The source_woodlot column groups colonies by collection site but, per the data description, is background information that does not make any row a repeat of another; the report treats woodlot tallies as descriptive only and applies no test to them.","observed_value":"Woodlot is a grouping label, not a repeated-measures indicator; woodlot tallies are untested","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":22,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"Every colony was tested a single time, so the file holds no repeated measurements of\nthe same colony: the 20 rows are 20 independent observations, one per colony. The\nwoodlot label is background information about where a colony came from and does not\nturn any row into a repeat of another row."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":34,"end_line":35,"quoted_text":"Woodlot tallies are descriptive; they are not tested. The single test above\nuses one observation per colony, which is the independent unit of this study."}]},{"description":"The reported statistics were independently recomputed from the raw data and match: 15 of 20 colonies chose the narrow cavity (proportion 0.75), and the exact two-sided binomial p-value against p = 0.5 is 0.041389, confirming the test consumed each of the 20 independent rows exactly once with no inflated trial count.","observed_value":{"successes":15,"n":20,"proportion":0.75,"p_value":0.041389},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":19,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"- Colonies choosing narrow: 15 of 20\n- Observed proportion choosing narrow: 0.7500\n- Exact two-sided p-value: 0.041389"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any path through which one colony could enter the binomial test more than once: (1) scanned all 20 CSV rows for duplicate colony_id values and found none (TMN-01 through TMN-20 each appear exactly once); (2) checked whether the test's trial count (n_rows = 20) could exceed the number of distinct independent units and found n_rows equals the distinct colony_id count of 20; (3) checked whether the per-woodlot tallies are re-fed into any inferential procedure that would double-count colonies and found they are only formatted into a descriptive table with no test applied; (4) verified the workflow's uniqueness guard would abort execution on any repeated colony_id, so the produced report could not have been generated from data with repeated units. Every attempt to establish repeated independent-unit entry failed.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}